<urn:usf:acceptance:architecture-conformance> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A conforming verdict is a statement about structure at one population digest. It is not a claim that the implementation behaves correctly, that a reachable unit is ever executed, or that an unreachable unit has no consumer outside this repository." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:architecture-conformance> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The foundation architecture is declared in current terms, including every surface implementation is legitimately entered through. Every implementation unit in the declared population carries exactly one classification with zero unaccounted and zero unexplained orphans. Every requirement in the foundation architecture assurance set is decided against a corpus observation of the exact tree, the release claim composes that set and fails closed without it, and each declared adversarial verification is shown to produce its expected disposition and then removed." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
