<urn:usf:architecture-conformance-disposition:conforming> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionMeaning> "Every requirement in the set was decidable at the observed scope and held." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-conformance-disposition:conforming> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:ArchitectureConformanceDisposition> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-conformance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "architecture-conformance" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-conformance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Declaring a population does not measure one. The graph states which units are in scope and how they are enumerated; the count, the reachability and the classification of each unit are observations, and a verdict that carries no observation is missing evidence rather than a pass." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-conformance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "No orphan-finding type is introduced. An orphan is an implementation unit whose classification is declared non-conforming, and the finding is the failing requirement that reports it. A parallel finding type would have carried the same fact in a second place." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-conformance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "No tool is named anywhere in this extension. An enforcement binding names the repository modules that produce an observation, and those modules are replaceable evidence producers: substituting a compiler-backed or third-party analyser changes the evidence and leaves every requirement, classification and verdict definition untouched." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-conformance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Nothing here is a second proof system. Requirement, Evidence, EvidenceClass, EvidenceRequirement, ProofObligation, ProofAlgorithm, ProofResult, RealisationPermission, WorkPacket, ValidationRuntimeClosure, IntegrityInvariant and the whole architecture-assurance vocabulary are reused unchanged; an architecture verdict travels the same evidence and proof machinery as every other claim in this corpus." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture-conformance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Make a declared architecture decidable. The architecture-assurance extension gave USF the vocabulary to state a topology; this one adds what was missing to measure an implementation against it: the roots reachability starts from, the population the claim is made over, the classifications an unreachable unit may legitimately carry, the scope an observation covers, and the composition that lets a release claim depend on an assurance set and fail closed when its evidence is absent." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
