<urn:usf:architecture:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Declaring a layer does not make the implementation acyclic. Fourteen units sit in import cycles today and are enumerated as a bounded exception, which is measured debt rather than intent: the exception may shrink and a cycle reaching any other unit is a violation." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The foundation declares no ports and no adapters, because it is not a ports-and-adapters architecture. The vocabulary carries both and a product profile in this corpus instantiates them; their absence here is a fact about the foundation rather than a gap in the model." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "This describes the foundation as measured, not as wished for. Several permitted directions are ones a stricter architecture would forbid: the realisation and provider layers both reach the command surface, and the semantic layer reaches the realisation layer. They are declared because they are true. Tightening one to a forbidden direction is an architecture change with its own work, not a correction to this declaration." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:architecture:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "The foundation stated as its own rules. USF is a module architecture rather than a ports-and-adapters one: a primitives centre, a semantic layer over it, a realisation layer that carries work through the lifecycle, a provider layer, an operations layer and one command surface, with a bootstrap loop above the surface it drives." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
