<urn:usf:contract:architecture-conformance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The permitted writes are three exact files and one narrow prefix. A conformance evaluator that could write the command, provider or realisation machinery it evaluates would be able to change its own subject." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:contract:architecture-conformance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Turn a declared architecture into a decidable one. The vocabulary to state a topology existed and was instantiated for a product only; the foundation had never stated its own, so nothing could measure whether the implementation matched it. This contract declares the foundation architecture, the population every claim is made over, the roots reachability starts from and the classifications an unreachable unit may carry, and supplies a replaceable observer and an evaluator that reads every decision from the graph." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:contract:architecture-conformance:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Measured 2026-09-04 before the work. The architecture-assurance vocabulary held twenty types and forty-two predicates and had zero foundation instances: one product had instantiated it and the foundation never had. A first reachability observation over src/ alone found 167 units, 93 reachable from the four declared command roots and 74 from none: 64 product capability modules and ten foundation modules. Nine of the ten had a declaration explaining them. The tenth appeared unexplained until the denominator was widened to recipes/, which holds a declared build-time recipe that imports it; declaring that root is what the finding actually called for." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
