<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:product-realisation-root:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "product-realisation-root" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:product-realisation-root:1> <urn:usf:predicate:classifiesAs> <urn:usf:implementation-classification:product-declared> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:product-realisation-root:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionOwner> "the product realisation profile that writes this root" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:product-realisation-root:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionReason> "Realised capability implementations are written beneath this root by a product profile through the ordinary transaction path. Whether a capability module is reachable, how it is layered and what it may import are that profile's decisions. The foundation accounts for these units and defers judgement on them, which is a different thing from excluding them: an exclusion would leave them out of the denominator, and a denominator with a hole in it proves nothing." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:product-realisation-root:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionRoot> "src/capabilities/" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:product-realisation-root:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Deferring judgement is not deferring accounting. These units are counted, and the foundation still asserts that none of its own implementation depends on them." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:product-realisation-root:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:ImplementationDispositionDecision> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "superseded-contribution-chain" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:classifiesAs> <urn:usf:implementation-classification:superseded-retained> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionOwner> "the semantic consolidation closure, which recorded the retention on 2026-09-02" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionReason> "These are the early composable-envelope primitives. The consolidation closure dispositioned them as superseded and deliberately retained, for the completed works that own the chain and as historical evidence of how contribution identity was first expressed. That decision existed only in a closed JSON record no mechanism reads, which is exactly how a retention becomes indistinguishable from an oversight; stating it here makes it a fact the assurance model can act on." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionSupersededBy> "the realisation basis, whose scoped dependency digest carries what an envelope digest was reaching for" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionUnit> "src/collaboration/index.ts" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionUnit> "src/core/dependencies.ts" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionUnit> "src/core/envelope.ts" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Retention is not permanent. This decision is the thing to revisit if the chain it serves is ever retired; until then the units are accounted for and nobody has to rediscover why they are here." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-disposition:superseded-contribution-chain:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:ImplementationDispositionDecision> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-population:foundation:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "foundation-implementation" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-population:foundation:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Tests, scripts and applications are outside this population and outside every claim made over it. They are not unchecked, they are the subject of other obligations. The one consumer relationship this leaves unmodelled is deliberate: a test importing foundation implementation exercises it and does not make it reachable." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-population:foundation:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "recipes/ is in the population because it holds implementation, not because it is convenient. A first enumeration covered src/ alone, which made a module a build-time recipe imports look like an orphan and very nearly justified deleting it. A denominator that stops short of a consumer is the same defect as a denominator that stops short of a subtree." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-population:foundation:1> <urn:usf:predicate:populationMemberSuffix> ".ts" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-population:foundation:1> <urn:usf:predicate:populationRoot> "recipes/" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-population:foundation:1> <urn:usf:predicate:populationRoot> "src/" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-population:foundation:1> <urn:usf:predicate:populationRule> "Every TypeScript module beneath src/ and recipes/, enumerated recursively, with no exclusion. A denominator with an exclusion is a denominator somebody can quietly widen; product implementation and assurance tooling are inside the population and carry a classification instead." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:implementation-population:foundation:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:ImplementationPopulation> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:module-boundary:assurance-tooling:1> <urn:usf:predicate:boundaryForbids> "No implementation unit of a declared component may import a module beneath src/architecture/. The observer would otherwise become part of what it observes, and a check that its own subject depends on can be made to pass by the code it is checking." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:module-boundary:assurance-tooling:1> <urn:usf:predicate:boundaryScope> "src/architecture/" <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:module-boundary:assurance-tooling:1> <urn:usf:predicate:boundaryScope> <urn:usf:architecture:1> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
