<urn:usf:module-boundary:assurance-tooling:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dependencyRuleReason> "Naming the scope is also what makes every source attributable: a unit is assigned to a component, covered by an excluded boundary, or unaccounted for. Without the boundary the honest count of unaccounted units could not be asserted to be zero, and an unaccounted unit is a hiding place." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:module-boundary:assurance-tooling:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Exclusion from the component model is not exemption from checking. Units in this scope are still enumerated, still classified, still counted in the denominator and still subject to every rule that does not depend on component assignment." <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
<urn:usf:module-boundary:assurance-tooling:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:ModuleBoundaryRule> <urn:usf:graph:architecture-conformance> .
